WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.137
Now we align the pandas dtypes more closely with the concepts.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:07.292
Sex becomes a categorical variable.

00:00:07.292 --> 00:00:15.302
Triage level and membership tier use ordered categorical dtypes with the intended order written explicitly.

00:00:15.302 --> 00:00:22.087
Patient ID becomes a string because it identifies a record rather than measuring an amount.

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:29.717
The dtype is now more informative, but it still does not replace documentation about the meaning of each

00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:35.797
variable. Preprocessing is not neutral: it tells software how to interpret the variable.

00:00:35.797 --> 00:00:43.322
One-hot encoding avoids inventing rank for nominal categories; ordinal coding preserves a known order;

00:00:43.322 --> 00:00:48.687
scaling changes numerical representation but not conceptual meaning.

00:00:48.687 --> 00:00:56.447
In predictive work, learned preprocessing should be fitted only on training data so evaluation remains honest.
